lls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Louisiana remains one of the most Republican-leaning states on the presidential map, backing the GOP by double digits in recent cycles. The 2028 race is open, with the incumbent term-limited and neither party's nominee settled. No public polls of the state or expert ratings exist this far out, so the forecast rests on the state's fundamental partisan lean.\n\nThe expected margin is roughly eleven points Republican, with wide uncertainty given the distance to Election Day and the absence of state polling. A strong Democratic nominee or a sharp national shift could narrow the gap, but recent history offers little precedent for Louisiana flipping in a normal presidential year. The race is rated Likely Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.108, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.162, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1608, "margin": -11.0}]}